# Vite copies this directory's contents byte-for-byte into dist/ at
# build time, and Vercel's build does NOT fetch Git LFS objects during
# its clone -- so anything here that matched frontend/.gitattributes'
# blanket "*.png filter=lfs" (and friends) shipped as a ~130-byte LFS
# pointer text file instead of the real asset, which a browser can't
# render as an image. Confirmed against the deployed site: the pointer
# text ("version https://git-lfs.github.com/spec/v1...") was exactly
# what Vercel served at /img/logo/lotsynclogo.png.
#
# A more specific .gitattributes overrides the parent for anything
# under this directory (git's normal precedence rule), so everything
# in public/ is unconditionally exempted from LFS, regardless of what
# extension-based rules frontend/.gitattributes adds in the future.
* -filter -diff -merge -text
